+# B5 — Used-game Business
+
+September 22, 2026. **B5 technically complete. Stop before B6. Owner acceptance pending; not beta ready.**
+
+Sellers now physically enter the shop, visit a separate intake, disclose condition-sensitive terms and negotiate a bounded cash acquisition. Rowan inspects and explicitly confirms the exact accepted payment. Each purchased copy keeps its own condition, label, acquisition cost and provenance through next-prep stocking, player/employee claims, fixed-price resale and financial reporting.
+
+## Candidate and preservation
+
+Branch `main`, HEAD `22ac1bcbf6f4cc65fd7425508a1f471e2306dff9`, **plus the uncommitted B1–B5 tree**. HEAD alone does not identify this candidate. B5 retained the [incoming full source manifest](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/incoming-manifest.json), [B1–B4 source/document/tracker archive](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/incoming-b1-b4.tar.gz) and [incoming working-tree status](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/incoming-status.txt) before edits. Earlier deliveries/evidence, artwork and editable masters remain intact.
+
+The [final source manifest](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/source-manifest.json) and [source snapshot](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/source-snapshot.tar.gz) identify delivered source, tests, documentation and the external root tracker. [Preservation and verification reconciliation](../../encounter/evidence/b5-20260922/preservation-check.json) binds executable bytes to the final [isolated validation context](../../encounter/evidence/validation-20260922T214753102202Z/context.json). Documentation finalized after execution is separately identified. No owner-save access, commit, push, publication or artwork/master overwrite occurred.
+
+## Delivered rules
+
+**Schema 9 / `b5-used-1`; namespace `game-sim-first-week-dev-v9`.** All older namespaces remain untouched. Incompatible saves reject before replacing live state, and cannot be overwritten by Save. The isolation wrapper refuses prior namespaces (including v8), missing/duplicate settings and disabled isolation before starting Godot. No migration is claimed. The optional historical full-shift capture tool now delegates isolation to the same checked wrapper instead of silently attempting an obsolete R5 namespace replacement. That legacy signed-app capture path was not executed; B5 footage uses the standard validator.
+
+| Area | Implemented behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| Interim content | Original Curb Circuit 02, Tidebound Atlas and Orbit Orchard only. New references remain $21.99/$27.99/$14.99. Existing three rotating buyers, six prepaid copies, overnight suppliers, layout/growth and staff rules remain. |
+| Seller arrival | One per open day from day 2, admitted after 12 shop seconds and clear entry. Day 2–7 sequence: C-good, O-fair, T-good, C-fair, O-good, T-worn. Terms materialize on Open, never reroll on reload. Sellers use intake (850,420), separate from buyer queue/cashier. Rowan walks to protected inspection (810,420). |
+| Valuation | Good/fair/worn use 80%/60%/40% of the unchanged new reference. Suggested resale is rounded down to cents; asking is floor(70% of resale), minimum floor(50%). B1’s future authored overrides and final references remain B6. |
+| Negotiation | Inspection exposes title, condition, suggested resale and asking. Offer $1–asking; one initial offer. Below floor reveals one seller counter; accept it or submit at most one final shop offer. Below-floor final is refused. An amount at/above floor is accepted **at that exact amount**; no automatic purchase or substitution with the floor. |
+| Payment | Separate Confirm purchase captures seller/day/revision/product/condition/accepted amount. State rechecks them, cash and backroom including inbound reservations before one synchronous debit/event/copy/resolution. Duplicate or stale confirmation is nonmutating. Insufficient money/space keeps the exact accepted offer pending with an explanation. A full display does not block available backroom space. |
+| Cancellation | Leave pending closes the dialog while retaining terms; explicit Refuse/Cancel resolves without payment/copy. Closing cancels all unpaid trades, including accepted-but-unconfirmed offers. Paid trades cannot be canceled. Visible sellers walk out; unadmitted sellers are canceled immediately. |
+| Individual inventory | One `used:<run>:<day>:1` unpriced backroom copy per paid seller, with condition, immutable accepted cost and acquisition event. Eligibility is next day’s preparation; same-day labeling, stock claims and resale are barred. New copies retain their own new condition/cost/provenance. |
+| Labels/allocation | Product-wide price controls affect **new** copies only. Copies / labels exposes each copy’s identity, kind, condition, location, cost and price, with acquisition-event tooltip. Explicit individual labels and exact-copy Shelf +1 travel through receiving/rack controls. Workers use the same existing stock claims. New/used reservations cannot share a copy or slot. |
+| Resale | Existing rotating preferences and stable copy-selection order remain; no substitution or extra customers. At reservation, the selected used copy’s buyer budget scales by its condition percentage, rounds down, and locks with the fixed label/decision. Buyers pay that label or decline; no shopper negotiation. |
+| Reporting | Used purchases add inventory-at-cost and cash stock spending. They do not enter cost of sales until the specific copy sells. That sale retains its actual accepted acquisition cost. Margin is sale receipts minus sold-copy cost; wages, investment and cash are separate. |
+| Recovery/close | Save retains negotiation history, terms, resolution, seller motion/position, copy provenance, buyer reservations and work history. Restoration validates first, cancels unfinished execution claims and reconstructs travel without recreating stock or payments. Closing drains visible sellers, admitted buyers and checkout work before existing exactly-once wage/rent settlement. Terminal phases reject trading/labeling/stocking. |
+
+`used.gd` owns the seller rules and independently reconstructs expected acquisitions from completed trades/events; `state.gd` retains shared transaction, inventory and validation authority. `main.gd` supplies ordinary controls and physical travel. The new inspector port participates in shared layout reachability. Every actor participates in movement clearance. Artwork is reused unchanged; this is functional seller presentation, not B7 animation acceptance.
